/**
@defgroup api Public API
@brief Everything reachable from `#include <batchlas.hh>`, plus the two opt-in SYCL headers.

Every entry point enqueues on a batchlas::Queue and returns a batchlas::Event;
nothing is readable until the queue (or the event) is waited on. The backend is
taken from the Queue, options are designated-initialiser structs, and scratch
comes from the Queue's workspace arena. The conventions shared by all entry
points are in @ref md_docs_2cpp-api.

@{

@defgroup core Queues, devices and events
@brief batchlas::Queue, batchlas::Device, batchlas::Event and SYCL interop.

@defgroup matrix Matrices, views and vectors
@brief Column-major batched containers and the non-owning views every entry point takes.

@defgroup enums Enumerations and scalar concepts
@brief Transpose, Uplo, Side, Diag, Backend and the scalar concepts that constrain every template.

@defgroup options Option structs
@brief Designated-initialiser option structs accepted by the entry points.

@defgroup blas2 BLAS level 2
@brief Batched matrix-vector operations.

@defgroup blas3 BLAS level 3
@brief Batched matrix-matrix operations: gemm, trsm, trmm, symm/hemm, syrk/herk, syr2k/her2k.

@defgroup factorizations Factorizations and linear solvers
@brief Cholesky and LU factorizations, their solves and inverses.

@defgroup qr QR and orthogonal transforms
@brief Householder QR, forming and applying Q, and batched orthogonalisation.

@defgroup eigen Symmetric and Hermitian eigensolvers
@brief syev and its tiers, selected-range syevx, and the iterative eigensolvers.

@defgroup tridiag Tridiagonal and band reduction
@brief Reduction to tridiagonal form and the tridiagonal eigensolvers (steqr, stedc, stebz, stein).

@defgroup svd Singular value decomposition
@brief gesvd and the bidiagonal pipeline stages.

@defgroup sparse Sparse (CSR) operations
@brief Sparse-dense products, ILU(k) and CSR test-matrix generators.

@defgroup extra Norms, condition numbers and utilities
@brief Matrix norms, condition estimates, inversion and scaling helpers.

@defgroup linalg Convenience layer (batchlas::linalg)
@brief Value-returning, NumPy-like wrappers over the entry points.

@defgroup dispatch Dispatch and routing
@brief How a call picks a Route{Origin, Algorithm}: RouteTable, supports(), preferred(), env overrides.

Design record: @ref md_docs_2design_2vendor-independence. Measurements behind
each window: @ref perf_evidence.

@defgroup workspace Workspace and memory
@brief The per-Queue workspace arena, leases and BumpAllocator sizing.

@defgroup errors Errors and convergence status
@brief The exception hierarchy and per-item info reporting.

@defgroup config Configuration, environment and tuning
@brief Runtime settings captured from the environment and the tuning constants.

@defgroup device Device-side group BLAS
@brief In-kernel work-group and sub-group BLAS templates (`#include <batchlas/blas/device.hh>`, needs `-fsycl`).

@defgroup internal_helpers Kernel helpers (installed, not API)
@brief Headers installed because public headers include them. Not a stable interface.

@}
*/
